# The thread transcripts stay local: they are verbatim internal discussion, not a
# publication artefact (Mike, 2026-09-13 06:50 UTC). Nothing under chat/ ever
# enters history, which is the property a repo that will later go public needs.
chat/

# scratch / local
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# built views: regenerated by tools/backlog/build.py, never hand-edited
backlog.html
graph.html
graph.json
# built view: regenerated by tools/atlas/build.py; a page full of result values, so it is
# never committed and is off limits to a blind v2 author (ADR-003)
atlas.html

# full-text copies with no confirmed redistribution licence (2026-09-13/14 import)
sources/local/

# Raw wave output written next to the launcher. Until 2026-09-18 the runnable tree
# lived in a session scratchpad, so nights 1-4 wrote these outside the repository and
# no rule was needed; the venv now sits at tools/.venv and the launcher's --out-dir is
# its own directory, so night 5 onwards writes here. These are the raw artefacts -- a
# per-run json/log/stdout.log triple of ~8.6 MB each, plus the wave's pid, progress and
# launcher logs. None has ever been in history: the repository keeps the distilled
# results/ tree instead. Ignored rather than committed so that a wave in flight cannot
# make the tree dirty, which is the state a pre-registration's own guard refuses to run
# in (S52, autoresearch-win-rtx: an un-gitignored cache tripped the dirty-guard and the
# runner had never once run).
tools/night/*.json
tools/night/*.log
tools/night/wave_*.pid

# Row B (night 5), raw per-checkpoint outputs stay out of git (Zcode, 2026-09-20/21).
# The per-checkpoint activity-profile csvs and per-run step h5 files are raw data, not
# distilled results: hundreds of MB across the ten runs, regenerated bit-for-bit from
# the committed rowB.py on the recorded driver/library stack (results/night5/diagnostics/
# rowB/instrument_stack.json), never hand-edited, and never an input a later reading is
# allowed to pool silently. See README.md's "raw outputs stay out of git" paragraph.
# Scoped to results/night5/ only: nights 2 and 3's rowB directories already carry
# similarly-named files in history (git ls-files checked, 2026-09-20/21) --
# `rowB_profiles_250008.csv`, `rowB_profiles_25212.csv`, `rowB_profiles_iter0.csv` under
# results/night2/diagnostics/rowB and results/night3/diagnostics/rowB -- and a repo-wide
# pattern would shadow those already-tracked files. Nothing here untracks anything.
results/night5/diagnostics/rowB/**/rowB_profiles_*.csv
results/night5/diagnostics/rowB/**/rowB_floor_profiles_*.csv
results/night5/diagnostics/rowB/**/rowB_steps_*.h5
results/night5/diagnostics/rowB/**/rowB_floor_steps_*.h5
